IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulations 18 to 20: the risk assessments a relevant person makes (money laundering and terrorist financing, regulation 18;
-- proliferation financing, regulation 18A), the policies, controls and procedures it keeps (regulations 19 and 19A), and what a relevant
-- parent undertaking does for its group (regulation 20).
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- Each function answers a question of the form "has the relevant person done what this paragraph requires?" (see mlr1-reg16-17-authorities).
-- Whether the person is a relevant person at all is the question of regulation 8 (module 1); the seat gates every question here on it.

§ `Regulation 18 -- Risk assessment by relevant persons`

-- reg 18(1).  A relevant person must take appropriate steps to identify and assess the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to
-- which its business is subject.
-- src:484 | (1) A relevant person must take appropriate steps to identify and assess the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject.
@ref reg 18(1) (src:484-484)
GIVEN `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject` AND `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must take appropriate steps to identify and assess the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing to which its business is subject" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 18(2).  In carrying out the risk assessment the relevant person must take into account (a) information made available by the
-- supervisory authority under regulations 17(9) and 47, and (b) risk factors including factors relating to its customers, the countries
-- or geographic areas in which it operates, its products or services, its transactions and its delivery channels.
-- SEAM S-2 (answering side of the asking in regulations 33, 35, 37): the information is an input of the core types.
-- src:485 | (2) In carrying out the risk assessment required under paragraph (1), a relevant person must take into account—
-- src:486 | (a) information made available to them by the supervisory authority under regulations 17(9) and 47, and
-- src:487 | (b) risk factors including factors relating to—
-- src:488 | (i) its customers;
-- src:489 | (ii) the countries or geographic areas in which it operates;
-- src:490 | (iii) its products or services;
-- src:491 | (iv) its transactions; and
-- src:492 | (v) its delivery channels.
@ref reg 18(2) (src:485-492)
GIVEN `it has taken into account the information made available to it by the supervisory authority under regulations 17(9) and 47` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its customers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to the countries or geographic areas in which it operates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its products or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its delivery channels` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18(2) the relevant person has taken into account what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken into account the information made available to it by the supervisory authority under regulations 17(9) and 47` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its customers` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to the countries or geographic areas in which it operates` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its products or services` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its transactions` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its delivery channels` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person must take into account—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 18(3).  In deciding what steps are appropriate under paragraph (1), the relevant person must take into account the size and nature of its business.
-- src:493 | (3) In deciding what steps are appropriate under paragraph (1), the relevant person must take into account the size and nature of its business.
@ref reg 18(3) (src:493-493)
GIVEN `it has taken into account the size of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account the nature of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18(3) the relevant person has taken into account the size and nature of its business` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken into account the size of its business` AND `it has taken into account the nature of its business` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant person must take into account the size and nature of its business" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 18(4).  A relevant person must keep an up-to-date record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1), unless its
-- supervisory authority notifies it in writing that such a record is not required.
-- src:494 | (4) A relevant person must keep an up-to-date record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1), unless its supervisory authority notifies it in writing that such a record is not required.
@ref reg 18(4) (src:494-494)
GIVEN `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18(4) the relevant person has kept the record paragraph (4) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "its supervisory authority has notified it in writing that such a record is not required"
        IF `it keeps a record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)` AND `the record is up to date` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must keep an up-to-date record in writing of all the steps it has taken under paragraph (1)" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 18(5).  A supervisory authority may not give the notification referred to in paragraph (4) unless it considers that the risks of
-- money laundering and terrorist financing applicable to the sector in which the relevant person operates are clear and understood.
-- src:495 | (5) A supervisory authority may not give the notification referred to in paragraph (4) unless it considers that the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing applicable to the sector in which the relevant person operates are clear and understood.
@ref reg 18(5) (src:495-495)
GIVEN `the supervisory authority considers that the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing applicable to the sector in which the relevant person operates are clear and understood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18(5) the supervisory authority may give the notification referred to in paragraph (4)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the supervisory authority considers that the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing applicable to the sector in which the relevant person operates are clear and understood` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A supervisory authority may not give the notification referred to in paragraph (4) unless it considers that the risks ... are clear and understood"

-- reg 18(6).  A relevant person must provide the risk assessment, the information on which it was based and any record required under
-- paragraph (4) to its supervisory authority on request.
-- src:496 | (6) A relevant person must provide the risk assessment it has prepared under paragraph (1), the information on which that risk assessment was based and any record required to be kept under paragraph (4), to its supervisory authority on request.
@ref reg 18(6) (src:496-496)
GIVEN `it has provided the risk assessment it has prepared under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has provided the information on which that risk assessment was based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has provided any record required to be kept under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its supervisory authority has requested them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18(6) the relevant person has provided what paragraph (6) requires on request` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`its supervisory authority has requested them`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "its supervisory authority has requested them" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has provided the risk assessment it has prepared under paragraph (1)` AND `it has provided the information on which that risk assessment was based` AND `it has provided any record required to be kept under paragraph (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must provide the risk assessment it has prepared under paragraph (1), the information on which that risk assessment was based and any record required to be kept under paragraph (4), to its supervisory authority on request" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

§ `Regulation 18A -- Risk assessment by relevant persons in relation to proliferation financing`

-- reg 18A(1).  A relevant person must take appropriate steps to identify and assess the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject.
-- src:498 | (1) A relevant person must take appropriate steps to identify and assess the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject.
@ref reg 18A(1) (src:498-498)
GIVEN `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18A(1) the relevant person has taken the steps paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken appropriate steps to identify the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject` AND `it has taken appropriate steps to assess those risks` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must take appropriate steps to identify and assess the risks of proliferation financing to which its business is subject" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 18A(2).  In carrying out the risk assessment the relevant person must take into account (a) information in the report referred to
-- in regulation 16A, and (b) risk factors including factors relating to its customers, geographic areas, products or services, transactions and delivery channels.
-- src:499 | (2) In carrying out the risk assessment required under paragraph (1), a relevant person must take into account—
-- src:500 | (a) information in the report referred to in regulation 16A (risk assessment by the Treasury); and
-- src:501 | (b) risk factors including factors relating to—
-- src:502 | (i) its customers;
-- src:503 | (ii) the countries or geographic areas in which it operates;
-- src:504 | (iii) its products or services;
-- src:505 | (iv) its transactions; and
-- src:506 | (v) its delivery channels.
@ref reg 18A(2) (src:499-506)
GIVEN `it has taken into account information in the report referred to in regulation 16A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its customers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to the countries or geographic areas in which it operates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its products or services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its transactions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its delivery channels` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 18A(2) the relevant person has taken into account what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has taken into account information in the report referred to in regulation 16A` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its customers` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to the countries or geographic areas in which it operates` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its products or services` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its transactions` AND `it has taken into account risk factors relating to its delivery channels` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a relevant person must take into account—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 18A(3).  In deciding what steps are appropriate, the relevant person must take into account the size and nature of its business.
