        IF NOT (`its supervisory authority has requested them`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "its supervisory authority has requested them" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has provided the risk assessment it has prepared under paragraph (1)` AND `it has provided the information on which that risk assessment was based` AND `it has provided any record required to be kept under paragraph (4)` THEN JUST TRUE
