§ `Regulation 19 -- Policies, controls and procedures`

-- reg 19(1).  A relevant person must (a) establish and maintain policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the
-- risks identified in its regulation 18(1) assessment; (b) regularly review and update them; (c) maintain a record in writing of them, of changes
-- made on review, and of the steps taken to communicate them within the business.
-- src:511 | (1) A relevant person must—
-- src:512 | (a) establish and maintain policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing identified in any risk assessment undertaken by the relevant person under regulation 18(1);
-- src:513 | (b) regularly review and update the policies, controls and procedures established under sub-paragraph (a);
-- src:514 | (c) maintain a record in writing of—
-- src:515 | (i) the policies, controls and procedures established under sub-paragraph (a);
-- src:516 | (ii) any changes to those policies, controls and procedures made as a result of the review and update required by sub-paragraph (b); and
-- src:517 | (iii) the steps taken to communicate those policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within the relevant person's business.
@ref reg 19(1) (src:511-517)
GIVEN `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of money laundering and terrorist financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18(1)` AND `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` AND `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` AND `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` AND `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19(2).  The policies, controls and procedures must be (a) proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the business, and (b) approved by senior management.
-- src:518 | (2) The policies, controls and procedures adopted by a relevant person under paragraph (1) must be—
-- src:519 | (a) proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the relevant person's business, and
-- src:520 | (b) approved by its senior management.
@ref reg 19(2) (src:518-520)
GIVEN `the policies, controls and procedures are proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the relevant person's business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policies, controls and procedures are approved by its senior management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(2) the policies, controls and procedures are proportionate and approved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the policies, controls and procedures are proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the relevant person's business` AND `the policies, controls and procedures are approved by its senior management` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The policies, controls and procedures adopted by a relevant person under paragraph (1) must be—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19(3).  The policies, controls and procedures must include (a) risk management practices; (b) internal controls (regulations 21 to 24);
-- (c) customer due diligence (regulations 27 to 38); (d) reliance and record keeping (regulations 39 to 40); (e) the monitoring and
-- management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, the policies.
-- src:521 | (3) The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include—
-- src:522 | (a) risk management practices;
-- src:523 | (b) internal controls (see regulations 21 to 24);
-- src:524 | (c) customer due diligence (see regulations 27 to 38);
-- src:525 | (d) reliance and record keeping (see regulations 39 to 40);
-- src:526 | (e) the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, such policies, controls and procedures.
@ref reg 19(3) (src:521-526)
GIVEN `they include risk management practices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include internal controls` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include customer due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include reliance and record keeping` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, such policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(3) the policies, controls and procedures include what paragraph (3) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they include risk management practices` AND `they include internal controls` AND `they include customer due diligence` AND `they include reliance and record keeping` AND `they include the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, such policies, controls and procedures` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19(4)(a) to (d).  The policies, controls and procedures must include policies which (a) provide for the identification and scrutiny of
-- unusual transactions and other high-risk activity; (b) specify additional measures against anonymity; (c) ensure new products and
-- technology are assessed; (d) require anyone in the organisation who knows or suspects money laundering to comply with Part 3 of the
-- Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002.
-- src:527 | (4) The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include policies, controls and procedures—
-- src:528 | (a) which provide for the identification and scrutiny of—
-- src:529 | (i) any case where—
-- src:530 | (aa) a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large in each case given the nature of the transaction, or there is an unusual pattern of transactions, or
-- src:531 | (bb) the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose, and
-- src:532 | (ii) any other activity or situation which the relevant person regards as particularly likely by its nature to be related to money laundering or terrorist financing;
-- src:533 | (b) which specify the taking of additional measures, where appropriate, to prevent the use for money laundering or terrorist financing of products and transactions which might favour anonymity;
-- src:534 | (c) which ensure that when new products, new business practices (including new delivery mechanisms) or new technology are adopted by the relevant person, appropriate measures are taken in preparation for, and during, the adoption of such products, practices or technology to assess and if necessary mitigate any money laundering or terrorist financing risks this new product, practice or technology may cause;
-- src:535 | (d) under which anyone in the relevant person's organisation who knows or suspects (or has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting) that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing as a result of information received in the course of the business or otherwise through carrying on that business is required to comply with—
-- src:536 | (i) Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 ; or
-- src:537 | (ii) Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 ;
@ref reg 19(4) (src:527-537)
GIVEN `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any case where a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, or there is an unusual pattern of transactions, or the transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any other activity or situation which the relevant person regards as particularly likely by its nature to be related to money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they specify the taking of additional measures, where appropriate, to prevent the use for money laundering or terrorist financing of products and transactions which might favour anonymity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they ensure that when new products, new business practices or new technology are adopted, appropriate measures are taken in preparation for, and during, the adoption to assess and if necessary mitigate any money laundering or terrorist financing risks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they require anyone in the relevant person's organisation who knows or suspects that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing to comply with Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(4)(a) to (d) the policies, controls and procedures include policies as paragraph (4) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any case where a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, or there is an unusual pattern of transactions, or the transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` AND `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any other activity or situation which the relevant person regards as particularly likely by its nature to be related to money laundering or terrorist financing` AND `they specify the taking of additional measures, where appropriate, to prevent the use for money laundering or terrorist financing of products and transactions which might favour anonymity` AND `they ensure that when new products, new business practices or new technology are adopted, appropriate measures are taken in preparation for, and during, the adoption to assess and if necessary mitigate any money laundering or terrorist financing risks` AND `they require anyone in the relevant person's organisation who knows or suspects that a person is engaged in money laundering or terrorist financing to comply with Part 3 of the Terrorism Act 2000 or Part 7 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include policies, controls and procedures—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19(4)(e).  In the case of a money service business that uses agents, the policies must ensure that appropriate measures are taken by
-- the business to assess (i) whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58, and
-- (ii) the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing.
-- SEAM S-4 (asking): regulation 58 (module mlr3) answers whether the agent satisfies the fit and proper test.
-- src:538 | (e) which, in the case of a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business, ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess—
-- src:539 | (i) whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58; and
-- src:540 | (ii) the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref reg 19(4)(e) (src:538-540)
GIVEN `reg 58 the agent satisfies the fit and proper test` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(4)(e)(i) the agent would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58` MEANS `reg 58 the agent satisfies the fit and proper test`

-- src:538 | (e) which, in the case of a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business, ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess—
-- src:539 | (i) whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58; and
-- src:540 | (ii) the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing.
@ref reg 19(4)(e) (src:538-540)
GIVEN `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(4)(e) the policies, controls and procedures of a money service business that uses agents include what sub-paragraph (e) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant person is a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58` AND `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for money laundering or terrorist financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which, in the case of a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business, ensure that appropriate measures are taken" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19(5).  In determining what is appropriate or proportionate, a relevant person may take into account any guidance issued by the FCA, or
-- issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.  Guidance from elsewhere is not named.
-- src:541 | (5) In determining what is appropriate or proportionate with regard to the size and nature of its business, a relevant person may take into account any guidance which has been—
-- src:542 | (a) issued by the FCA; or
-- src:543 | (b) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury.
@ref reg 19(5) (src:541-543)
GIVEN `the guidance has been issued by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance has been issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the guidance has been approved by the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(5) the relevant person may take the guidance into account` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance has been issued by the FCA` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the guidance has been issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body` AND `the guidance has been approved by the Treasury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a relevant person "may take into account any guidance which has been— (a) issued by the FCA; or (b) issued by any other supervisory authority or appropriate body and approved by the Treasury"; the paragraph says nothing of other guidance

-- reg 19(6).  A relevant person must, where relevant, communicate the policies, controls and procedures to its branches and subsidiary
-- undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom.
-- src:544 | (6) A relevant person must, where relevant, communicate the policies, controls and procedures which it establishes and maintains in accordance with this regulation to its branches and subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom.
@ref reg 19(6) (src:544-544)
GIVEN `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its branches located outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its subsidiary undertakings located outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has branches or subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19(6) the relevant person has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its branches and subsidiary undertakings outside the United Kingdom` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it has branches or subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "it has branches or subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its branches located outside the United Kingdom` AND `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its subsidiary undertakings located outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must, where relevant, communicate the policies, controls and procedures which it establishes and maintains in accordance with this regulation" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

§ `Regulation 19A -- Policies, controls and procedures in relation to proliferation financing`

-- reg 19A(1).  A relevant person must (a) establish and maintain policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the
-- risks of proliferation financing identified in its regulation 18A(1) assessment; (b) regularly review and update them; (c) maintain a record in writing.
-- src:546 | (1) A relevant person must—
-- src:547 | (a) establish and maintain policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of proliferation financing identified in any risk assessment undertaken by the relevant person under regulation 18A(1);
-- src:548 | (b) regularly review and update the policies, controls and procedures established under sub-paragraph (a);
-- src:549 | (c) maintain a record in writing of—
-- src:550 | (i) the policies, controls and procedures established under sub-paragraph (a);
-- src:551 | (ii) any changes to those policies, controls and procedures made as a result of the review and update required by sub-paragraph (b); and
-- src:552 | (iii) the steps taken to communicate those policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within the relevant person’s business.
@ref reg 19A(1) (src:546-552)
GIVEN `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of proliferation financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(1) the relevant person has done what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has established and maintains policies, controls and procedures to mitigate and manage effectively the risks of proliferation financing identified in its risk assessment under regulation 18A(1)` AND `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures` AND `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established` AND `it maintains a record in writing of any changes made as a result of the review and update` AND `it maintains a record in writing of the steps taken to communicate the policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, within its business` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19A(2).  The policies, controls and procedures must be (a) proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the business, and (b) approved by senior management.
-- src:553 | (2) The policies, controls and procedures adopted by a relevant person under paragraph (1) must be—
-- src:554 | (a) proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the relevant person’s business; and
-- src:555 | (b) approved by its senior management.
@ref reg 19A(2) (src:553-555)
GIVEN `the policies, controls and procedures are proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the relevant person's business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policies, controls and procedures are approved by its senior management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(2) the policies, controls and procedures are proportionate and approved` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the policies, controls and procedures are proportionate with regard to the size and nature of the relevant person's business` AND `the policies, controls and procedures are approved by its senior management` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The policies, controls and procedures adopted by a relevant person under paragraph (1) must be—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19A(3).  The policies, controls and procedures must include (a) risk management practices; (b) internal controls (regulations 21 to 24);
-- (c) the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, the policies.
-- src:556 | (3) The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include—
-- src:557 | (a) risk management practices;
-- src:558 | (b) internal controls (see regulations 21 to 24);
-- src:559 | (c) the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, such policies, controls and procedures.
@ref reg 19A(3) (src:556-559)
GIVEN `they include risk management practices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include internal controls` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they include the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, such policies, controls and procedures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(3) the policies, controls and procedures include what paragraph (3) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they include risk management practices` AND `they include internal controls` AND `they include the monitoring and management of compliance with, and the internal communication of, such policies, controls and procedures` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19A(4)(a) to (c).  The policies must include policies which (a) provide for the identification and scrutiny of unusual transactions and
-- other activity related to proliferation financing; (b) specify additional measures against anonymity; (c) ensure new products and technology are assessed.
-- src:560 | (4) The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include policies, controls and procedures—
-- src:561 | (a) which provide for the identification and scrutiny of—
-- src:562 | (i) any case where—
-- src:563 | (aa) a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large in each case given the nature of the transaction, or there is an unusual pattern of transactions; or
-- src:564 | (bb) the transaction or transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose, and
-- src:565 | (ii) any other activity or situation which the relevant person regards as particularly likely by its nature to be related to proliferation financing;
-- src:566 | (b) which specify the taking of additional measures, where appropriate, to prevent the use for proliferation financing of products and transactions which might favour anonymity;
-- src:567 | (c) which ensure that when new products, new business practices (including new delivery mechanisms) or new technology are adopted by the relevant person, appropriate measures are taken in preparation for, and during, the adoption of such products, practices or technology to assess and if necessary mitigate any proliferation financing risks this new product, practice or technology may cause;
@ref reg 19A(4) (src:560-567)
GIVEN `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any case where a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, or there is an unusual pattern of transactions, or the transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any other activity or situation which the relevant person regards as particularly likely by its nature to be related to proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they specify the taking of additional measures, where appropriate, to prevent the use for proliferation financing of products and transactions which might favour anonymity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they ensure that when new products, new business practices or new technology are adopted, appropriate measures are taken in preparation for, and during, the adoption to assess and if necessary mitigate any proliferation financing risks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(4)(a) to (c) the policies, controls and procedures include policies as paragraph (4) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any case where a transaction is unusually complex or unusually large, or there is an unusual pattern of transactions, or the transactions have no apparent economic or legal purpose` AND `they provide for the identification and scrutiny of any other activity or situation which the relevant person regards as particularly likely by its nature to be related to proliferation financing` AND `they specify the taking of additional measures, where appropriate, to prevent the use for proliferation financing of products and transactions which might favour anonymity` AND `they ensure that when new products, new business practices or new technology are adopted, appropriate measures are taken in preparation for, and during, the adoption to assess and if necessary mitigate any proliferation financing risks` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The policies, controls and procedures referred to in paragraph (1) must include policies, controls and procedures—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 19A(4)(d).  In the case of a money service business that uses agents, the policies must ensure that appropriate measures are taken to
-- assess (i) whether an agent would satisfy the fit and proper test in regulation 58, and (ii) the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for proliferation financing.
-- SEAM S-4 (asking): the same answer from regulation 58 as in regulation 19(4)(e).
-- src:568 | (d) which, in the case of a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business, ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess—
-- src:569 | (i) whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58; and
-- src:570 | (ii) the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for proliferation financing.
@ref reg 19A(4)(d) (src:568-570)
GIVEN `reg 58 the agent satisfies the fit and proper test` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(4)(d)(i) the agent would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58` MEANS `reg 58 the agent satisfies the fit and proper test`

-- src:568 | (d) which, in the case of a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business, ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess—
-- src:569 | (i) whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58; and
-- src:570 | (ii) the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for proliferation financing.
@ref reg 19A(4)(d) (src:568-570)
GIVEN `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relevant person is a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(4)(d) the policies, controls and procedures of a money service business that uses agents include what sub-paragraph (d) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the relevant person is a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the relevant person is a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business" (ruling 2026-11-05, (c): a scope limit with no "only")
        IF `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess whether an agent used by the business would satisfy the fit and proper test provided for in regulation 58` AND `they ensure that appropriate measures are taken by the business to assess the extent of the risk that the agent may be used for proliferation financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "which, in the case of a money service business that uses agents for the purpose of its business, ensure that appropriate measures are taken" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

