      `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its subsidiary undertakings located outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has branches or subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 19A(5) the relevant person has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its branches and subsidiary undertakings outside the United Kingdom` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it has branches or subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "it has branches or subsidiary undertakings which are located outside the United Kingdom" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its branches located outside the United Kingdom` AND `it has communicated the policies, controls and procedures to its subsidiary undertakings located outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant person must, where relevant, communicate the policies, controls and procedures which it establishes and maintains in accordance with this regulation" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

§ `Regulation 20 -- Policies, controls and procedures: group level`

-- reg 20(1).  A relevant parent undertaking must (a) ensure that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and
-- 19A(1) apply to all its subsidiary undertakings (including those outside the United Kingdom) and to any branches it has established outside
-- the United Kingdom, which carry out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations; (b) establish
-- and maintain throughout its group policies for data protection and for sharing information for the purposes of preventing money
-- laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing; (c) regularly review and update them; (d) maintain a record in writing.
-- src:573 | (1) A relevant parent undertaking must—
-- src:574 | (a) ensure that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and 19A(1) apply—
-- src:575 | (i) to all its subsidiary undertakings, including subsidiary undertakings located outside the United Kingdom; and
-- src:576 | (ii) to any branches it has established outside the United Kingdom;
-- src:577 | which is carrying out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations;
-- src:578 | (b) establish and maintain throughout its group the policies, controls and procedures for data protection and sharing information for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing with other members of the group , including policies on the sharing of information about customers, customer accounts and transactions;
-- src:579 | (c) regularly review and update the policies, controls and procedures applied and established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b);
-- src:580 | (d) maintain a record in writing of—
-- src:581 | (i) the policies, controls and procedures established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b);
-- src:582 | (ii) any changes to those policies, controls and procedures made as a result of the review and update required by sub-paragraph (c); and
-- src:583 | (iii) the steps taken to communicate those policies, controls and procedures, or any changes to them, to its subsidiary undertakings and branches.
@ref reg 20(1) (src:573-583)
GIVEN `it has ensured that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and 19A(1) apply to all its subsidiary undertakings, including those located outside the United Kingdom, which carry out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has ensured that those policies, controls and procedures apply to any branches it has established outside the United Kingdom which carry out such an activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has established and maintains throughout its group the policies, controls and procedures for data protection and for sharing information for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing with other members of the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures applied and established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established, of any changes made as a result of the review and update, and of the steps taken to communicate them to its subsidiary undertakings and branches` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 20(1) the relevant parent undertaking has done what paragraph (1) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it has ensured that the policies, controls and procedures referred to in regulations 19(1) and 19A(1) apply to all its subsidiary undertakings, including those located outside the United Kingdom, which carry out any activity in respect of which the relevant person is subject to these Regulations` AND `it has ensured that those policies, controls and procedures apply to any branches it has established outside the United Kingdom which carry out such an activity` AND `it has established and maintains throughout its group the policies, controls and procedures for data protection and for sharing information for the purposes of preventing money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing with other members of the group` AND `it regularly reviews and updates the policies, controls and procedures applied and established under sub-paragraphs (a) and (b)` AND `it maintains a record in writing of the policies, controls and procedures established, of any changes made as a result of the review and update, and of the steps taken to communicate them to its subsidiary undertakings and branches` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant parent undertaking must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 20(3).  If any of the subsidiary undertakings or branches of a relevant parent undertaking are established in a third country which does
-- not impose requirements as strict as those of the United Kingdom, the parent must ensure that they apply equivalent measures, as far as
-- permitted under the law of the third country.
-- src:585 | (3) If any of the subsidiary undertakings or branches of a relevant parent undertaking are established in a third country which does not impose requirements to counter money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing as strict as those of the United Kingdom, the relevant parent undertaking must ensure that those subsidiary undertakings and branches apply measures equivalent to those required by these Regulations, as far as permitted under the law of the third country.
@ref reg 20(3) (src:585-585)
GIVEN `it has ensured that those subsidiary undertakings and branches apply measures equivalent to those required by these Regulations, as far as permitted under the law of the third country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of its subsidiary undertakings or branches are established in a third country which does not impose requirements to counter money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing as strict as those of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 20(3) the relevant parent undertaking ensures that its third-country subsidiaries and branches apply equivalent measures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`any of its subsidiary undertakings or branches are established in a third country which does not impose requirements to counter money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing as strict as those of the United Kingdom`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "any of its subsidiary undertakings or branches are established in a third country which does not impose requirements to counter money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing as strict as those of the United Kingdom" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has ensured that those subsidiary undertakings and branches apply measures equivalent to those required by these Regulations, as far as permitted under the law of the third country` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant parent undertaking must ensure that those subsidiary undertakings and branches apply measures equivalent to those required by these Regulations" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 20(4).  Where the law of a third country does not permit the application of such equivalent measures, the parent must (a) inform its
-- supervisory authority accordingly, and (b) take additional measures to handle the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing.
-- src:586 | (4) Where the law of a third country does not permit the application of such equivalent measures by the subsidiary undertaking or branch established in that country, the relevant parent undertaking must—
-- src:587 | (a) inform its supervisory authority accordingly; and
-- src:588 | (b) take additional measures to handle the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing.
@ref reg 20(4) (src:586-588)
GIVEN `it has informed its supervisory authority that the law of the third country does not permit the application of equivalent measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has taken additional measures to handle the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law of a third country does not permit the application of such equivalent measures by the subsidiary undertaking or branch established in that country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 20(4) the relevant parent undertaking informs its supervisory authority and takes additional measures` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the law of a third country does not permit the application of such equivalent measures by the subsidiary undertaking or branch established in that country`) THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not arise: "the law of a third country does not permit the application of such equivalent measures by the subsidiary undertaking or branch established in that country" (ruling 2026-11-05, (b): a "where" condition not met; in a function that asks whether the requirement has been met, a duty that does not arise leaves nothing unmet, as in the "unless" of reg 18(4) and reg 21(3); fork F-where)
        IF `it has informed its supervisory authority that the law of the third country does not permit the application of equivalent measures` AND `it has taken additional measures to handle the risk of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the relevant parent undertaking must—" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 20(5).  A relevant parent undertaking must ensure that information relevant to the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing and
-- proliferation financing is shared as appropriate between members of its group, subject to any restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under any enactment or otherwise.
-- src:589 | (5) A relevant parent undertaking must ensure that information relevant to the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing is shared as appropriate between members of its group, subject to any restrictions on sharing information imposed by or under any enactment or otherwise.
@ref reg 20(5) (src:589-589)
GIVEN `it has ensured that information relevant to the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing is shared as appropriate between members of its group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sharing is restricted by or under any enactment or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 20(5) the relevant parent undertaking ensures that relevant information is shared between members of its group` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sharing is restricted by or under any enactment or otherwise` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement is displaced: "the sharing is restricted by or under any enactment or otherwise"
        IF `it has ensured that information relevant to the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing is shared as appropriate between members of its group` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A relevant parent undertaking must ensure that information relevant to the prevention of money laundering, terrorist financing and proliferation financing is shared as appropriate between members of its group" (Marginal readings, (c): a requirement not done is read as the text's no)

-- reg 20(6).  The FCA may make technical standards specifying (a) what additional measures are required from credit institutions and financial
-- institutions under paragraph (4); and (b) the minimum action to be taken by them where paragraph (4) applies.  A power: it is not an
-- obligation, and a standard on some other subject is not covered by it.
-- src:590 | (6) The FCA may make technical standards specifying—
-- src:591 | (a) what additional measures are required from credit institutions and financial institutions under paragraph (4); and
-- src:592 | (b) the minimum action to be taken by credit institutions and financial institutions where paragraph (4) applies.
@ref reg 20(6) (src:590-592)
GIVEN `the standards specify what additional measures are required from credit institutions and financial institutions under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the standards specify the minimum action to be taken by credit institutions and financial institutions where paragraph (4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 20(6) the FCA may make the technical standards` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the standards specify what additional measures are required from credit institutions and financial institutions under paragraph (4)` OR `the standards specify the minimum action to be taken by credit institutions and financial institutions where paragraph (4) applies` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the FCA "may make technical standards specifying— (a) ...; and (b) ..."; the paragraph says nothing of standards on any other subject
